hristian Lobby - Anti-discrimination laws","noes":41,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2016-05-04.133.2) introduced by Greens Senator [Robert Simms](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/sa/robert_simms). It called for the Prime Minister \"*to reject the [Australian Christian Lobby](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Christian_Lobby)'s request for a temporary suspension to the anti-discrimination laws should a plebiscite campaign on marriage equality eventuate*\". ### Wording of the motion > *That the Senate—* > *(a) acknowledges that the [Australian Christian Lobby](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Christian_Lobby) does not represent most Christians in this country and are nothing more than a fringe group;* > *(b) condemns the Treasurer ([Mr Morrison](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/cook/scott_morrison)) for attending the Australian Christian Lobby National Conference on 23 April 2016; and* > *(c) calls on the Prime Minister ([Mr Turnbull](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/wentworth/malcolm_turnbull)) to reject the Australian Christian Lobby's request for a temporary suspension to the anti-discrimination laws should a plebiscite campaign on marriage equality eventuate.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4248","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2016-05-04/5"}
